@startuml sequence_diagram_engine_failure
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - VIS01 Engine Failure and Cleanup (renderer creation, module build, frame update/render, context loss)

actor User as "Manager / Restaurant Staff"
participant Viewer as "KitchenViewer"
participant Engine as "ViewerEngine"
participant A as "Module A"
participant B as "Module B\n(fails)"
participant C as "Module C"
participant Three as "three\n(WebGLRenderer / Scene)"

note over User, Three
    Precondition: configuration valid and EVERY asset preloaded (sequence_diagram_open_viewer D2).
    Asset download failures never reach the engine: they are the "error / asset-unavailable" state (D1).
    On failure the engine calls dispose(). The viewer removes the canvas and shows Retry.
    Cleanup continues after individual errors and can be called again safely.
end note

== F1. Renderer creation fails ==

Viewer -> Engine : ViewerEngine.create(canvas, container, { onFatalError })
activate Engine
Engine -> Three : new WebGLRenderer({ canvas })
Three --> Engine : throws (context could not be created)
Engine -> Engine : dispose()  (resources allocated so far)
Engine --> Viewer : throw ViewerEngineError{ phase: "renderer" }
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Viewer : assets.dispose()\ncanvas.remove()
Viewer --> User : ViewerStatusMessage("failed") + [Retry]
note right of Viewer : no module created, loop never started

== F2. A module build fails (sync throw or rejected Promise) ==

Viewer -> Engine : await engine.load(configuration, assets, [makeA, makeB, makeC], signal)
note right of Engine : load() takes ownership of loadedAssets first
activate Engine
Engine -> A : modules.push(A); await A.build(ctx)
activate A
A --> Engine : done
deactivate A
Engine -> B : modules.push(B)  (registered BEFORE build)\nawait B.build(ctx)
activate B
B --> Engine : throws / rejects
deactivate B
note right of Engine : C is never created nor built
Engine -> Engine : dispose()
group dispose()
    Engine -> Engine : mark disposed; running = false
    Engine -> Three : setAnimationLoop(null)
    Engine -> Engine : abort build controller; disconnect resize observer;\nremove context listener
    Engine -> B : dispose()  (must be safe after a partial build)
    activate B
    B --> Engine : throws
    deactivate B
    Engine -> Engine : collect error, CONTINUE
    Engine -> A : dispose()
    activate A
    A --> Engine : ok
    deactivate A
    Engine -> Three : traverse scene: dispose remaining\ngeometries / materials / textures (each once)
    Engine -> Engine : loadedAssets.dispose()
    Engine -> Three : renderer.dispose(); renderer.forceContextLoss()
    Engine -> Engine : report collected cleanup errors
end
Engine --> Viewer : throw ViewerEngineError{ phase: "build", moduleName: "B" }
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Viewer : engine.dispose()  (already disposed)\ncanvas.remove()
Viewer --> User : ViewerStatusMessage("failed") + [Retry]\n"The 3D viewer stopped because of an error."

== F3. update() or render() throws during the render loop ==

Viewer -> Engine : start()  (after a successful load of A, B, C)
activate Engine
Engine -> Three : render first frame; setAnimationLoop(frame)
Three -> Engine : frame(t)
Engine -> A : update(dt)
Engine -> B : update(dt)
activate B
B --> Engine : throws
deactivate B
Engine -> Engine : fatal(error) calls dispose()\n(C, B, A disposed in reverse order)
Engine -> Viewer : onFatalError(ViewerEngineError{ phase: "update", moduleName: "B" })
deactivate Engine
note right of Engine : reported ONCE; a frame callback already queued\nsees running == false and returns.\nrender() throwing follows the same path (phase "render").
Viewer -> Viewer : canvas.remove()
Viewer --> User : ViewerStatusMessage("failed") + [Retry]

== F4. WebGL context lost (driver reset, GPU memory pressure) ==

Three -> Engine : event "webglcontextlost"
activate Engine
Engine -> Engine : preventDefault(); fatal(error) calls dispose()
Engine -> Viewer : onFatalError(ViewerEngineError{ phase: "context" })
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Viewer : canvas.remove()
Viewer --> User : ViewerStatusMessage("failed") + [Retry]

== F5. Unmount or reload while a build is still pending ==

note over Viewer, Engine : The effect assigns its local engine variable\nbefore awaiting load().
Viewer -> Viewer : cleanup calls controller.abort()
Viewer -> Engine : abort listener calls dispose()
activate Engine
Engine -> Engine : stop loop, abort build controller\nand release owned resources
Engine -> B : build signal aborted
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Engine : engine.dispose()  (already disposed)
Viewer -> Viewer : canvas.remove()
note right of B : When a dependency resolves late, the module\nchecks the signal and releases the result.
B --> Engine : pending build settles
activate Engine
Engine -> Engine : sweepScene() releases remaining scene resources
Engine --> Viewer : load() returns false
deactivate Engine
note right of Viewer : The aborted signal prevents the attempt\nfrom starting the engine or updating the UI.

== Retry ==

User -> Viewer : clicks Retry
Viewer -> Viewer : clean up; set loading; increment attempt
Viewer -> Viewer : check WebGL; request configuration; preload assets
Viewer -> Viewer : createElement("canvas"); append to viewport
Viewer -> Engine : ViewerEngine.create(newCanvas, ...)
note right of Viewer : a canvas after forceContextLoss() is never reused;\nthe fresh canvas receives a new WebGL context

@enduml
